Regression guard: an OCaml binding name may end in a prime (`inputView'`),
which is a legal, idiomatic identifier character but illegal in a CSS
identifier. The class is a hash of the module, scope, binding name and
content, so the binding name never appears in it and the selector is valid
CSS.

  $ refmt --parse re --print ml input.re > output.ml
  $ ../../standalone.exe --impl output.ml -o output.ml
  $ styled-ppx.generate output.ml > styles.css

  $ cat styles.css
  /* This file is generated by styled-ppx, do not edit manually */
  .css-1grx60o{position:absolute;}
